{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1116526-entropy-mage-20th","id":1116526,"title":"Entropy, mage 20th.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-15T13:06:03-07:00","id":1116526,"title":"Entropy, mage 20th.","content":"I've been wondering about Mage 20th entropic usage, the rank 2 of the previous titles allowed the character to use a certain application called &quot;Begginer's luck&quot; which could, for each success in the arete roll adds an automatic success on a random action of the player's choosing. I haven't found anything about this spell in M20 or How do you Do that, I might be blind and overlooked it but I re-read this twice.<br /> <br /> Was this spell negated on M20 or is it usable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T13:33:10-07:00","id":1116533,"title":"","content":"My view is that M20's sphere page assumes prior knowledge with the sphere system and as such does not bother explaining itself with examples.<br /> <br /> There are many things omitted from the spheres section that make no sense to leave out such as how healing works with Life.<br /> <br /> So unless M20 outright contradicts something from a previous edition, chances are it's assumed to carry over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-15-2017, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T14:12:43-07:00","id":1116553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1116526-entropy-mage-20th?p=1116533#post1116533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is that m29's sphere page assumes prior knowledge with the sphere system and as such does not bother explaining itself with examples.<br /> <br /> There are many things omitted from the spheres section that make no sense to leave out such as how healing works with Life.<br /> <br /> So unless M20 outright contradicts something from a previous edition, chances are it's assumed to carry over.</div> </div> </div> </div> So there's no definitive answer to this, other than assuming it works the same way? I mean, there are some stuff that aren't changed in M20 just re-written in a fancier way, and when they left that out I got curious. I mean, with the sphere's usage you can alter the odds to allow you to succeed at such actions but I was just making sure. I summon <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> because she's been by far the only person to give a definitive answer regarding such manners.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help, Saikou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T14:44:51-07:00","id":1116563,"title":"","content":"I remember it from Mage 2e. Checked my Mage we PDF copy and it's on page 212. You get one success per success added to any non-magical skill you have two dice or less or less to attempt with. Further uses are at +1 difficulty, because well, you aren't a beginner for long.<br /> <br /> So, you could get more than one success and make 'a lucky shot.' Given how many people believe in beginner's luck and lucky shots, it's probably coincidental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T19:38:24-07:00","id":1116643,"title":"","content":"It's really important to check the Common Magickal Effects charts starting on M20 page 508. Most of the sample rotes in the previous core books were moved there.<br /> <br /> Alter Probability is there as Entropy 2, which is what the concept of Beginners Luck is about.<br /> <br /> However I would say that M20 contradicts the specific rules of that sample rote. There's no reason Beginner's Luck in M20 should provide successes but with stipulations. M20 would consider the idea of beginner's luck as a Mythic Thread to pull on to add to a basic boosting of a roll effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T21:19:50-07:00","id":1116696,"title":"","content":"I'd concur with Heavy Arms. Beginner's Luck is a pretty standard Entropy 2 effect, so I don't see a need to use different rules than the M20 rules.<br /> <br /> Mage has evolved over the years and rotes were always a tricky thing, because if you make them very specific than the powers of mages resemble static spells in other games. So, when going back, look at rotes as suggestions on one way to achieve a desired effect. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}